---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Sources & Data Providers | Food Supply Crisis Report" description="Primary data and trusted institutions used for food supply, food security, agriculture, climate and price reporting."
  showAds={false}>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Research Sources</p>
    <h1>Sources & Data Providers</h1>
    <p>Our core source layer includes organizations that publish food, agriculture, climate, economic and humanitarian data.</p>
    <p>Sources are chosen for the specific question being answered. The organizations below publish original data, assessments or technical guidance; their material is not interchangeable, and a source link should be read with its publication date and geographic scope in mind.</p>
    <h2>How to choose the right source</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>World production, trade and commodity prices:</strong> start with FAO data and the monthly Cereal Supply and Demand Brief.</li>
      <li><strong>Acute hunger and humanitarian need:</strong> check current WFP and IPC assessments for the specific affected population and period.</li>
      <li><strong>National prices, stocks and crops:</strong> use the relevant national statistics office, agriculture ministry or official food agency.</li>
      <li><strong>Weather and climate:</strong> use the official meteorological or climate service, then check crop-condition evidence as the season progresses.</li>
      <li><strong>Household emergency guidance:</strong> follow the relevant local public-health and emergency authorities; guidance can differ by country and situation.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="card"><h2><a href="https://www.fao.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FAO</a></h2><p>Food production, markets, prices, agriculture and food security.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h2><a href="https://www.wfp.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WFP</a></h2><p>Hunger, food assistance and acute food insecurity.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h2><a href="https://www.ipcinfo.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IPC</a></h2><p>Acute food insecurity classification and analysis.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h2><a href="https://www.worldbank.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">World Bank</a></h2><p>Food systems, poverty, economic conditions and resilience.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h2><a href="https://www.ers.usda.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">USDA ERS</a></h2><p>US food prices, agriculture and food-system research.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h2><a href="https://www.noaa.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA</a></h2><p>Climate and weather information relevant to agriculture.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h2><a href="https://www.fao.org/worldfoodsituation/csdb" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FAO Cereal Supply and Demand Brief</a></h2><p>Monthly cereal production, utilization, trade and stock outlooks; check its release date because forecasts can be revised.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h2><a href="https://www.fao.org/worldfoodsituation/foodpricesindex/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FAO Food Price Index</a></h2><p>International commodity-price trends and group indices. It is not a direct consumer-price index for any one country.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h2><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/statistics/united-kingdom-food-security-report-2024" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">UK Defra Food Security Report</a></h2><p>Official analysis of global availability, UK supply sources, supply-chain resilience and household-level food security.</p></article>
      <article class="card"><h2><a href="https://www.cdc.gov/water-emergency/about/how-to-create-and-store-an-emergency-water-supply.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CDC emergency water guidance</a></h2><p>Practical US public-health guidance for creating and storing an emergency drinking-water supply; follow local guidance where you live.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
